This plugin implements the method of Digital Earth Australia Coastlines:

  Bishop-Taylor R., Nanson R., Sagar S., Lymburner L. (2021). Mapping
  Australia's dynamic coastline at mean sea level using three decades of
  Landsat imagery. Remote Sensing of Environment, 267, 112734.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rse.2021.112734

Parts of the computational core were ported from the DEA Coastlines source
code (Geoscience Australia, https://github.com/GeoscienceAustralia/dea-coastlines),
which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that
licence is in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Files that contain ported and modified code:

  core/composites.py   follows the raster stage of DEA Coastlines
                       (coastlines/raster.py)
  core/masks.py        port of contours_preprocess (coastlines/vector.py)
  core/rates.py        port of points_on_line, annual_movements,
                       change_regress, calculate_regressions and
                       all_time_stats (coastlines/vector.py) and of the
                       summary points from coastlines/continental.py

Changes made to the ported code:

  - rewritten for numpy, scipy and GDAL arrays instead of xarray,
    Open Data Cube and geopandas;
  - sizes of morphological elements converted from Landsat pixels to metres;
  - tide modelling replaced with an optional user-supplied sea level table;
  - the sea is found from the data (largest water body, all water bodies
    wider than 300 m, or a user layer) instead of a ready-made mask;
  - an alternative outlier rule (residuals from a Theil-Sen line) added.
